# 18.9 Implementation Plan — Slug Deep Link No-Expand & Anti-Flicker Hardening

## 🎯 Objective

Verify and harden the deep link slug feature (`#raid-N` URL → scroll to card + faint glow) so that:
1. Cards are **never force-expanded** when navigating via a slug URL.
2. The glow animation is **never flickery** due to competing CSS transitions or missing GPU compositing hints.

---

## 🔍 Issues Found in Audit

### Issue 1: `scrollToRaid()` force-opened `<details>` card  
**File:** `app.js` lines 200–203 (pre-fix)  
**Problem:** `scrollToRaid()` unconditionally set `card.open = true` before scrolling. The user requested that visiting `#raid-N` only scrolls and glows — no auto-expansion.

### Issue 2: `renderRaids()` auto-opened targeted card on initial render  
**File:** `app.js` `renderRaids()`, `card.open` logic (pre-fix)  
**Problem:** On first render, the card matching `#raid-N` or `pendingRaidScroll` was forced open via `card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id) || isTargetedRaid`. Same problem.

### Issue 3: `transition: none !important` dropped from `.raid-card.highlighted`  
**File:** `style.css` `.raid-card.highlighted` rule (pre-fix)  
**Problem:** Previously added in session 18.3/18.4, this critical rule was absent. Without it, the base `.raid-card` transition (`transform 0.3s, border-color 0.3s, box-shadow 0.3s`) competes with `@keyframes highlightPulse`, causing subpixel paint jank on the initial frames of the glow.

### Issue 4: `will-change` and `backface-visibility` missing  
**File:** `style.css` `.raid-card.highlighted` rule (pre-fix)  
**Problem:** GPU compositing hints also dropped. These promote the card to its own compositing layer, ensuring the box-shadow animation is painted without layout reflows.

---

## ✅ Changes Applied

### `app.js` — Remove card auto-open from `scrollToRaid()`
```js
// BEFORE
if (card.tagName.toLowerCase() === 'details' && !card.open) {
    isProgrammaticScrollOpening = true;
    card.open = true;
    setTimeout(() => { isProgrammaticScrollOpening = false; }, 80);
}
card.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });

// AFTER
card.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
// (no force-open; card stays in whatever state it was)
```

### `app.js` — Remove auto-open from `renderRaids()` initial render
```js
// BEFORE
if (hasRenderedBefore) {
    card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id);
} else {
    const isTargetedRaid = (pendingRaidScroll === raid.Raid_Num) ||
        (window.location.hash === `#raid-${raid.Raid_Num}`);
    card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id) || isTargetedRaid;
}

// AFTER
// Never force-open from URL slug — slugs are scroll+glow only.
card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id);
```

### `style.css` — Restore anti-flicker properties on `.raid-card.highlighted`
```css
/* BEFORE */
.raid-card.highlighted {
    animation: highlightPulse 2.1s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) forwards;
    z-index: 10;
    border-color: var(--accent) !important;
}

/* AFTER */
.raid-card.highlighted {
    transition: none !important;
    animation: highlightPulse 2.1s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) forwards;
    z-index: 10;
    border-color: var(--accent) !important;
    will-change: box-shadow;
    backface-visibility: hidden;
    -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
}
```

---

## ✔️ Verification

| Check | Result |
| :--- | :--- |
| `node -c app.js` syntax check | ✅ Exit 0, no errors |
| `scrollToRaid()` no longer calls `card.open = true` | ✅ Confirmed |
| `renderRaids()` no longer uses `isTargetedRaid` to force-open | ✅ Confirmed |
| `.raid-card.highlighted` has `transition: none !important` | ✅ Confirmed |
| `.raid-card.highlighted` has `will-change: box-shadow` | ✅ Confirmed |
| `animationend` guard (`e.target !== card`) still present | ✅ Confirmed |
| Idempotent pulse guard still present | ✅ Confirmed |

# Walkthrough — Slug Deep Link No-Expand & Anti-Flicker Hardening

We audited the deep link slug feature (`#raid-N` in the URL → scroll to that raid card + faint glow highlight) against the records in `doc/prompts/` and found three regressions that were reintroduced after the original 18.3–18.6 flicker-fix sessions. All three are now resolved.

---

## 🔍 What Was Wrong

### 1. Cards Were Being Force-Expanded on Deep Link
Both `scrollToRaid()` and `renderRaids()` contained code that opened the `<details>` element whenever a slug URL was used:

- **`scrollToRaid()`** explicitly did `card.open = true` before scrolling.
- **`renderRaids()`** (initial render path) evaluated `isTargetedRaid` and ORed it into `card.open`.

The user's requirement is: slugs **only** scroll and glow. The card's collapsed/expanded state should be independent and untouched.

### 2. `transition: none !important` Was Missing from `.raid-card.highlighted`
The base `.raid-card` rule carries a 0.3s CSS `transition` on `transform`, `border-color`, and `box-shadow`. When the `@keyframes highlightPulse` animation begins animating those same properties, the browser's transition engine and animation engine compete, causing a brief subpixel jitter on the first few frames.

This `transition: none !important` override was first added in session **18.3** (Flicker Fix), but had been dropped from the current code.

### 3. GPU Compositing Hints Were Also Missing
`will-change: box-shadow` and `backface-visibility: hidden` were also first added in 18.3 and subsequently dropped. Without them, the browser may rasterize the card's glow during the main thread paint cycle rather than on the compositor thread, increasing the risk of jank during page load when the main thread is busy.

---

## 🛠️ Changes Made

### [`app.js`](file:///d:/GitHub/[oU1TS]/events/app.js) — `scrollToRaid()`: removed force-open
```js
// Removed these 4 lines entirely:
if (card.tagName.toLowerCase() === 'details' && !card.open) {
    isProgrammaticScrollOpening = true;
    card.open = true;
    setTimeout(() => { isProgrammaticScrollOpening = false; }, 80);
}
```
The card now simply `scrollIntoView()` and gets `.highlighted` applied — open state untouched.

### [`app.js`](file:///d:/GitHub/[oU1TS]/events/app.js) — `renderRaids()`: removed `isTargetedRaid` auto-open
```js
// Before:
if (hasRenderedBefore) {
    card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id);
} else {
    const isTargetedRaid = ...;
    card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id) || isTargetedRaid;
}

// After (simplified):
card.open = openCardIds.has(card.id);
```

### [`style.css`](file:///d:/GitHub/[oU1TS]/events/style.css) — `.raid-card.highlighted`: restored anti-flicker CSS
```css
.raid-card.highlighted {
    transition: none !important;          /* ← restored: stops transition competing with keyframe */
    animation: highlightPulse 2.1s cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1) forwards;
    z-index: 10;
    border-color: var(--accent) !important;
    will-change: box-shadow;              /* ← restored: GPU compositing hint */
    backface-visibility: hidden;          /* ← restored: promotes to compositor layer */
    -webkit-backface-visibility: hidden;
}
```

---

## ✅ Verification

| Check | Result |
| :--- | :--- |
| `node -c app.js` syntax check | ✅ Exit 0 — clean |
| Deep link no longer force-opens card | ✅ `card.open = true` removed from `scrollToRaid()` |
| Initial render no longer force-opens card via slug | ✅ `isTargetedRaid` branch removed from `renderRaids()` |
| CSS transition isolation restored | ✅ `transition: none !important` back in `.raid-card.highlighted` |
| GPU compositing hints restored | ✅ `will-change` + `backface-visibility` back |
| Guarded `animationend` listener still in place | ✅ `e.target !== card` guard confirmed |
| Idempotent pulse guard still in place | ✅ Early-return if already highlighted + timer active |
| `stopHighlightAnimation()` correctly clears class + timer | ✅ Confirmed |
